Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:27:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 526/526] Tests: B12X's own preparation tests skip without B12X

Eighteen tests of the B12X preparation driver and coordinator (progress
aggregation, tuning shards and their consolidation and cancellation, winner
artifacts, tuning caches, the declaration dump, collective profiling) build
B12X's own preparation objects, directly or through the coordinator tests'
_tuning_progress helper. They now skip, as vLLM's other B12X tests do, when
the b12x package is not installed. The driver's and coordinator's other
tests, which a deployment without B12X still runs (no units, the control
exchanges), are unchanged.
---
 tests/model_executor/test_b12x_warmup.py |  2 ++
 tests/v1/executor/test_b12x_startup.py   | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

